      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are highlighting a very real tension between policy ideals and ground-level economic reality. When a mandated wage causes a small, essential local business to close, it can absolutely harm the very community and the very workers the policy intended to help. This is why policy often requires nuance, such as phased implementation or local variations, to bridge the gap between the \"ideal moral goal\" and the \"actual economic reality\" for small business owners.",
      "source": "target",
